"Live screen" = "Live screen";

/* Documentation sheet, Microphone section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**Send phone mic** makes this phone the camera's audio in OBS — a wireless mic. The **Microphone** row beneath it picks which one — Auto follows iOS's own routing; a headset or Bluetooth mic takes over on its own." = "**Send phone mic** makes this phone the camera's audio in OBS — a wireless mic. The **Microphone** row beneath it picks which one — Auto follows iOS's own routing; a headset or Bluetooth mic takes over on its own.";

/* Documentation sheet, Microphone section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**Auto lip-sync** sends the mic only as a timing reference for aligning your real microphone; it's never heard." = "**Auto lip-sync** sends the mic only as a timing reference for aligning your real microphone; it's never heard.";

/* Documentation sheet, Microphone section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"One mic, one role — turning one on turns the other off." = "One mic, one role — turning one on turns the other off.";

/* Documentation sheet, Screen mirror section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"Streams your whole screen, with app audio, to a **LensLink Screen** source — great for mobile games or app demos. iOS mutes DRM audio (Apple Music, Netflix), and your microphone isn't sent — mic yourself in OBS as usual. On iOS 27 and later, **Mirror Screen** uses the system screen-sharing picker, and mirroring keeps running in the background until you stop it (from LensLink or the system's screen-sharing indicator)." = "Streams your whole screen, with app audio, to a **LensLink Screen** source — great for mobile games or app demos. iOS mutes DRM audio (Apple Music, Netflix), and your microphone isn't sent — mic yourself in OBS as usual. On iOS 27 and later, **Mirror Screen** uses the system screen-sharing picker, and mirroring keeps running in the background until you stop it (from LensLink or the system's screen-sharing indicator).";

/* Documentation section header */
"Screen mirror" = "Screen mirror";

/* Documentation sheet, Options section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**Focus on faces** keeps focus and exposure on the faces the camera sees while focus is on auto, the way the Camera app does — a tap on the picture outranks it until the scene changes, and a lock ignores it. Off, the camera weights the centre of the frame." = "**Focus on faces** keeps focus and exposure on the faces the camera sees while focus is on auto, the way the Camera app does — a tap on the picture outranks it until the scene changes, and a lock ignores it. Off, the camera weights the centre of the frame.";

/* Documentation sheet, Options section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**Remote start from OBS**: while the app is open and idle, OBS can start the camera for you. The phone stays awake while it waits — locking it or leaving the app ends remote start. Siri: \"Start streaming with LensLink.\"" = "**Remote start from OBS**: while the app is open and idle, OBS can start the camera for you. The phone stays awake while it waits — locking it or leaving the app ends remote start. Siri: \"Start streaming with LensLink.\"";

/* Documentation sheet, Options section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**Idle view** is what the Live screen becomes 10 seconds after you last touch it, for a phone that's mounted and out of reach. **Standard** leaves the controls up. **Clean feed** hides everything but the picture — turn Stats on (status pill) before you stop touching it to keep the health readout. **Dim screen** blanks the screen and drops the brightness to save battery, and is the only one that also dims remote-start standby, a minute in. Any tap brings the controls back." = "**Idle view** is what the Live screen becomes 10 seconds after you last touch it, for a phone that's mounted and out of reach. **Standard** leaves the controls up. **Clean feed** hides everything but the picture — turn Stats on (status pill) before you stop touching it to keep the health readout. **Dim screen** blanks the screen and drops the brightness to save battery, and is the only one that also dims remote-start standby, a minute in. Any tap brings the controls back.";

/* Documentation sheet, Options section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**Pause** holds a stream without ending it — the phone stays connected, the camera stays on, and OBS shows a dimmed, blurred still with a pause symbol instead of a frozen picture. The pause button sits on the Live screen next to Stop, and the same control is in OBS (source properties) and the web panel. Audio keeps going, so the phone can still be your microphone while the picture is held." = "**Pause** holds a stream without ending it — the phone stays connected, the camera stays on, and OBS shows a dimmed, blurred still with a pause symbol instead of a frozen picture. The pause button sits on the Live screen next to Stop, and the same control is in OBS (source properties) and the web panel. Audio keeps going, so the phone can still be your microphone while the picture is held.";

/* Documentation sheet, Options section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**High frame rate** is experimental: it adds 120 and 240 fps to the Format sheet where this camera has them (1080p and 720p on recent iPhones; 240 uses a sensor-binned format). The stream's bitrate grows with it, the phone runs hotter and drains faster, and an OBS canvas set to 60 shows every other frame at best — set the canvas to match, and prefer USB. Turning it off drops the rate back to 60." = "**High frame rate** is experimental: it adds 120 and 240 fps to the Format sheet where this camera has them (1080p and 720p on recent iPhones; 240 uses a sensor-binned format). The stream's bitrate grows with it, the phone runs hotter and drains faster, and an OBS canvas set to 60 shows every other frame at best — set the canvas to match, and prefer USB. Turning it off drops the rate back to 60.";

/* Documentation sheet, Options section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**Remember camera settings** keeps each camera's exposure, white balance, zoom and focus from one stream to the next — a shot dialled in once stays dialled in, per lens. Turn it off and every camera starts on auto, and what was stored is forgotten." = "**Remember camera settings** keeps each camera's exposure, white balance, zoom and focus from one stream to the next — a shot dialled in once stays dialled in, per lens. Turn it off and every camera starts on auto, and what was stored is forgotten.";

/* Documentation sheet, Options section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"**Allow system video effects** is experimental: it lets iOS lower the frame rate on its own, which the Control Center video effects (Portrait, Studio Light) may require. Takes effect when the camera next starts." = "**Allow system video effects** is experimental: it lets iOS lower the frame rate on its own, which the Control Center video effects (Portrait, Studio Light) may require. Takes effect when the camera next starts.";

/* Documentation sheet, Tally light section (Markdown: keep the ** markers) */
"The colored border around the Live screen while streaming. Colors, priority order, and per-status off switches are customizable in Options → Tally light. The wave button beside a color makes that status pulse instead of holding steady — motion catches the eye for something you're meant to notice without watching for it." = "The colored border around the Live screen while streaming. Colors, priority order, and per-status off switches are customizable in Options → Tally light. The wave button beside a color makes that status pulse instead of holding steady — motion catches the eye for something you're meant to notice without watching for it.";

/* Documentation sheet, Tally light section (Markdown: keep the ** markers); %lld%% = the low-battery threshold (20%) */
"**Low battery** is one of the statuses you can light: it turns on with iOS Low Power Mode, or at %lld%% and below, and clears the moment you plug in. While the screen is dimmed the battery level also shows large under the wake hint — so a phone across the room can be read at a glance, without touching it." = "**Low battery** is one of the statuses you can light: it turns on with iOS Low Power Mode, or at %lld%% and below, and clears the moment you plug in. While the screen is dimmed the battery level also shows large under the wake hint — so a phone across the room can be read at a glance, without touching it.";

